<DetailLayout
  title="Research made easier to explore."
  eyebrow="Parkinson's project"
  intro="The first major goal is an AI-assisted knowledge resource that helps patients, families, and curious readers explore Parkinson's research and prepare better questions for healthcare professionals."
>
  <section>
    <h2>Parkinson's: our first initiative.</h2>
    <p>
      The first major goal is to develop an AI-assisted Parkinson's knowledge
      resource that can organize credible research, preserve source citations
      and limitations, and explain complex information in language patients and
      families can use when learning about the disease and preparing questions
      for healthcare professionals.
    </p>
    <p>
      The intended direction is AI-assisted research discovery and explanation,
      with source-linked outputs, citations, provenance, limitations, and
      uncertainty visible. Comparing findings should help people ask better
      questions, not delegate medical answers to an autonomous system.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Clear limits</h2>
    <p>
      The current question tool is an API prototype, not the founder's existing
      custom GPT. No verified research library is connected. Answers may be
      incomplete, incorrect, or out of date and should be checked independently.
    </p>
    <p>
      These tools are being explored as educational and research technologies.
      They are not intended to diagnose Parkinson's, prescribe treatment, or
      replace medical care.
    </p>
    <p>This website is not enrolling a study or collecting health records.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/#knowledgebase"
      >Explore Ask Parkinson's Insights <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
    >
  </section>
</DetailLayout>
